  "term": "porphyria",
  "definition": "Porphyria is a group of metabolic disorders caused by problems in the body’s heme-making pathway in the liver, bone marrow, or both. These conditions may be inherited or acquired and can involve neurological symptoms in acute forms or skin lesions in cutaneous forms.",
